{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/4bih8bm5","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":72,"top":520,"width":1040,"height":72},"text":"We repeat the same calculation many times and compare the average result with an ideal reference.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#525252","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/taq846","slideIndex":1,"text":"Keep the explanation simple: the project does not require the audience to know quantum mechanics. A measurement is an average from repeated simulated runs."}
