{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/i1xn67","slideIndex":6,"text":"The ideal-state fidelity projector is |psi><psi| for the noiseless output. We apply full PNA and SLC + PNA to that projector, then evaluate each corrected observable against the noisy density matrix. At 1x noise, raw fidelity is 0.695, full-PNA estimates 1.004, and SLC + PNA estimates 0.892. These approximate correction estimates can exceed the physical maximum of one; interpret them as near ideal rather than literal physical fidelities. The raw noisy-state fidelity is the exact simulator value."}
